Sir Arctos is a polar bear who gained speech and reason, a knight of the [[Org/Iridescent Church/index|Iridescent Church]]. He was brought from [[Geography/Austrene/index|Austrene]] and knighted by Aurelia VII, the Church's pontifex. He wears pearlescent plate over his fur, a purple cloak and a wide-brimmed hat, and carries a bastard sword and a shield. He keeps a monocle for poor sight in one eye, and calls himself a very smart bear. He eats from a bowl stamped with his name, using silver cutlery.

Anzu, meeting him, knew of no tribe of speaking polar bears and took him for either a druid who preferred the shape of a bear or an animal awakened by divine energy. He joined [[Org/Iconoclasm/index|Iconoclasm]] in the wake of the deaths at the [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Sableclutch/The Crowded Flea|Crowded Flea]].

In the white void above Save Your Soul Incorporated he asked [[Aut]] for one of his marks and took it on his chest. It hides by default and can be shown at will, will not appear to anyone who has already seen his bare skin without it, and shows on its own to anyone who has seen his skin with it. Aut offered to remove it, and does not compel his friends into his service.

Before the assault on the Gas-n-Go he had his sword silvered, and in the fane beneath it he dispelled the black cape that fought at Tywelwyn's shoulder.

Below the throne he went on into the deeper fane, and the [[Gas-n-Go Heart|Heart]] there named him one of the Poncho Boys. In the armory he took the white armband from its case, and [[People/Argyle|Argyle]]'s fortress shield, grappling gun and gold. When the gang's shift crew came at ten that night, the werebear among them swelled to fill the hall and pinned him against a wall.

After the fane he went with the others to the [[Org/Iridescent Church/Convox/Inquisition/index|Inquisition]]'s office and asked for the two Inquisitors [[Aut]] had named, Penitence and Absolution. In the questioning room below the lobby he told the story straight, and asked Inquisitor [[Org/Iridescent Church/Convox/Inquisition/People/Inquisitor Penitence|Penitence]] about joining the order; Penitence told him no ritual could be worked on an adult bear. He asked Penitence to carry word of their report to his friend Vane, and was refused.

He was bitten and seized by the [[Bestiary/Lovelorn|lovelorn]] in [[Org/Iridescent Church/Convox/Magical Crimes/People/Detective Ellis Brooks|Brooks]]'s flat, and one latched onto his face and would not let go until he knocked it off. He healed the others up afterwards. He casts [[Phenomena/Augury|augury]], and asked whether the Party should try to rescue Brooks; the answer came back as the four of them as zombies, and they let him go. That night he prayed to the [[Iridescent Host|Host]] and asked why he had been awakened when he could have stayed a sleeping bear, and got no answer.
